1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:05,117
The brush clears a carved throne. No one sits on it.

2
00:00:05,117 --> 00:00:14,105
This empty seat stands for the kings who ruled Magadha, one dynasty after another. Each one added land, and each one added power.

3
00:00:14,105 --> 00:00:16,970
Who sat on the throne of Magadha?

4
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:39,427
How do we know? Buddhist and Jain texts and the Puranas list the kings.

5
00:00:39,427 --> 00:00:47,922
Archaeologists dug up the walls of Rajgir and the wooden posts of Pataliputra. The exact dates of early kings are uncertain.

6
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:07,419
The first great dynasty of Magadha was the Haryanka.

7
00:01:07,419 --> 00:01:14,408
Bimbisara, from about 544 BCE by the traditional count, grew his kingdom by war and marriage.

8
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:23,773
He married princesses from Kosala, from the Licchavi clan and from Madra. He conquered Anga. His son Ajatashatru was bolder.

9
00:01:23,773 --> 00:01:30,143
He defeated Kosala and the Vajji republic. His army used a catapult and a covered war chariot.

10
00:01:30,143 --> 00:01:38,774
In his time, the first Buddhist council met. Udayin, his successor, founded Pataliputra at the meeting of the Ganga and Son.

11
00:01:38,774 --> 00:01:48,913
Next came the Shishunagas, who ended the power of Avanti. Then came the Nandas. Mahapadma Nanda is called ekarat, the sole ruler.

12
00:01:48,913 --> 00:01:54,539
The Nandas had great wealth and an enormous army, which Greek writers describe with awe.

13
00:01:54,539 --> 00:02:03,672
The last Nanda, Dhana Nanda, was overthrown about 321 BCE by Chandragupta Maurya. A new empire was about to begin.

14
00:02:19,483 --> 00:02:25,759
Old name, new name. The early capital of Magadha was Rajagriha, the royal house.

15
00:02:25,759 --> 00:02:32,961
Its ruins are at the modern town of Rajgir, in Bihar. The name has hardly changed, only shortened.

16
00:02:48,783 --> 00:02:56,486
Carve this tip into memory. Haryanka, Shishunaga, Nanda:. three families, one rising state.

17
00:02:56,486 --> 00:03:03,998
Three dynasties in order, and Bimbisara and Ajatashatru for the first. That covers most questions.

18
00:03:19,817 --> 00:03:36,612
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which dynasty did Bimbisara belong to? The answer: the Haryanka dynasty. Number two.

19
00:03:36,612 --> 00:03:55,909
Who founded Pataliputra? The answer: Udayin. Number three. Who overthrew the last Nanda king? The answer: Chandragupta Maurya.

20
00:03:55,909 --> 00:04:01,910
Now one line for Mains. Examine the factors behind the rise of Magadha.

21
00:04:21,717 --> 00:04:28,963
The empty throne goes into its case. It stands for the power of Magadha. Three facts to take away.

22
00:04:28,963 --> 00:04:42,065
An empty throne, symbol of power. Haryanka, Shishunaga, Nanda. Overthrown about 321 BCE. Next gallery: Persians and Alexander.

